SUMMARY:The Flying Ace (Richard E. Norman\, 1926) Centennial Screening
DESCRIPTION:This exciting silent film includes a robbery investigation\, 
 love story\, and Black pilots before they were legally allowed to earn li
 censes to fly in the United States! Our programming honors actor and stun
 tman\, Steve "Peg" Reynolds\, who had one leg.  On Wednesday\, October 7t
 h\, we'll host a pre-screening reception at the BFCA at 5:00 p.m.\, where
  The Richard E. Norman Collection (https://nam12.safelinks.protection.out
